     Deliberately no `display`: the tick is a flex row of box and label, and
     setting `display: block` here beat the utility class that made it one -
     which put the checkbox on a line of its own above its own wording. */
  .menu-item {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 14px;
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .menu-item:hover {
    background: var(--color-paper-raised);
